Day 34 (2026-10-27) - 3D models on the graphics card, navigation when a folder is missing or still being read (VersariteViewer 1.3)

Found in the project (written the evening before, no log): uGLStlDraw
(3D models drawn by the graphics card: vertex buffers, a GLSL shader,
the cut face closed with the stencil buffer), uGLRenderer.DrawModel,
TMView: the model live, the sharp picture by a thread
(TStlPictureThread); uDirectoryScanner: an urgent scan (climbing one
level up doesn't wait for the image being read); "Open file ...";
Combine GIFs: "scaled to the largest GIF".

1. Speed of the live model (user: "not nearly as fluid as my viewer").
   Measured with the same software OpenGL (llvmpipe) on the 180 000-
   triangle sphere: VersariteViewer 178 ms per frame, the STL viewer
   180 ms - the card's work is the same. So the rest:
   - uGLStlDraw: two shader programs. The one with "discard" (the cut,
     the picture's edges) keeps the card from skipping hidden fragments
     early; without a section the plain one is used, the picture's
     rectangle kept by the scissor test (uGLRenderer.DrawModel).
   - TMView: the sharp picture (copy, save, the filters' copy) only
     after the model has rested 1.5 s (was 0.4 s: a processor core
     between two turns), and not uploaded to the card while the model
     is drawn live (a 4K picture's upload made the next turn stutter).
   - uStlPanel.SetView: the panel drawn again only if a row changed (the
     turn is in no row; a drag changes the elevation by fractions of a
     degree - the whole panel was drawn and uploaded for every mouse
     move while it was open); TMView: while turning, at most every
     150 ms, the last value when the model rests.
   - The D line: "3D live: x ms per frame, n frames/s" (with D the
     card's time is measured to the end, glFinish), or "3D: pictures".
2. ImageToSave: a turned or cut model is saved / copied as set (it
   took the file's start view from the cache).
3. Navigation (user: "Not found" after the last session's folder was
   gone, and nothing reacted; while "scanning folders ..." the gestures
   did nothing):
   - HandleStartReady: a path that isn't there - the folder above it is
     tried, step by step through the scanner (TryParentOf; not for Total
     Commander's folder); the note says which was missing and where it
     browses instead.
   - Navigate: a step that can't be done yet because the folders are
     still being read is kept and done when the tree is there
     (FTreeStep; "the folders are still being read: the step follows").
   - ParentFolder with nothing open: up from the path asked for.
   Checked under Wine: start with C:\STL\missing\deeper opened C:\STL;
   up from C:\BIG\a_first (17 800 folders) and a gesture right during
   "scanning folders ..." landed in C:\BIG\b_second.
4. Slide show and Total Commander dir preview (user: with the dir
   preview on, the slide show played nothing): the pump stepped only
   the dir preview while it had a folder, and the dir preview waits
   while VersariteViewer is in front. Now the slide show overrides:
   PumpDeliveries steps the slide show first; switching it on ends a
   folder's preview (the show plays that folder); while it runs, Total
   Commander's cursor on a folder starts no preview; when it ends, the
   dir preview takes up the folder under the cursor again (asked afresh
   at the next poll). The info line and the "longer / shorter" note say
   "slide show" while it runs.
5. Release 1.3 (user: the STL view and the directory priorities work):
   tests TestNavigation 153, TestMouse 98, TestSort 172, TestStl 25,
   TestGifJoin 28, TestExtensions 80 - all pass; both editions build.
   Release notes 1.3 completed (the 3D view on the graphics card, the
   two ways to combine GIFs, Open file, the browsing fixes, the slide
   show over the dir preview), both readmes, the GitHub folder brought
   up to date (the viewer's sources, the tests, the docs).
6. Combine GIFs, "Scaled to largest GIF" hung the program (user): it ran
   on the UI thread, and every picture of the animation was composed
   and kept in memory before scaling (a long, large GIF: hundreds of MB,
   seconds to minutes with no reaction). Now uGifJoin composes, scales
   and encodes one picture at a time (TFrameComposer) and reports each
   frame (TGifJoinProgress, which can also cancel); TMView runs the
   joining on a thread (TGifJoinThread): the info line says "scaling
   frame n / m ... (Esc: cancel)", Esc cancels (no file left), the
   result is opened when done; a second Combine meanwhile is refused
   with a note. 40 frames of 64 x 48 scaled to 1600 x 1000: about 6 s,
   with the program reacting throughout. TestGifJoin 32 (progress once
   per frame, cancel leaves no file).
7. Started side by side ([Startup] Mode=2), Total Commander did not come
   (user; switching side by side off and on again started it): at the
   start it is told the last session's folder, which had been renamed
   (C:\projects\mview\...), and Total Commander stops at a folder that
   isn't there; later it is told the folder shown, which is. Now
   uTotalCommander.OpenInTotalCommander hands on only a folder that
   exists: the nearest one above it, else none.
8. Then (user: "better nothing at all should be passed to totalcmd, it
   has its own memory"): started side by side, Total Commander gets no
   folder at all (TMainForm.StartSideBySide, FSideAtStart); the menu
   entry later still hands it the folder shown. The check in
   OpenInTotalCommander (item 7) stays as a safety net.
9. Taken back (user: the cause was a VersariteViewer still running,
   hidden by the close protection in the taskbar - not the folder):
   started side by side, Total Commander is told the start folder again,
   as before (TMainForm.StartSideBySide; FSideAtStart removed). The
   check of item 7 stays: a folder that isn't there is not handed on.
